Approach (DFS)
We iterate through every cell in the grid. Whenever we encounter an unvisited land cell (1), we start a Depth-First Search (DFS) to explore its entire connected component and calculate its area.

The DFS function recursively visits all four neighboring cells (up, down, left, and right). If a cell is out of bounds, contains water (0), or has already been visited, it contributes 0 to the island's area. Otherwise, we mark the current cell as visited and recursively compute the area of its neighboring land cells.

The area of an island is calculated as:

1 for the current land cell, plus
the areas returned by the recursive DFS calls in all four directions.
After computing the area of an island, we update the maximum area found so far. Once every cell has been processed, the maximum recorded area is returned.

Algorithm
Initialize a visited set and a variable max_area to store the largest island area.

Traverse every cell in the grid.

If the current cell is land (1) and has not been visited:

Start a DFS from that cell.
Recursively visit all connected land cells.
Return the total area of the current island.
Update max_area with the larger of the current maximum and the computed area.
Return max_area.

Complexity Analysis
Time Complexity: O(m × n)

Every cell is visited at most once.
Space Complexity: O(m × n)

The visited set may store all land cells in the worst case, and the recursion stack can also grow to O(m × n) when the island spans the entire grid.
Code
class Solution:
    def maxAreaOfIsland(self, grid: List[List[int]]) -> int:
        rows = len(grid)
        cols = len(grid[0])
        visited = set()
        max_area = 0

        def dfs(r,c):
            if (r < 0 or r >= rows or c < 0 or c >= cols or
                grid[r][c] != 1 or (r,c) in visited):
                return 0
            visited.add((r,c))
            return (1 + dfs(r+1,c) +
                        dfs(r-1,c) +
                        dfs(r,c+1) +
                        dfs(r,c-1))

        for r in range(rows):
            for c in range(cols):
                if grid[r][c] == 1 and (r,c) not in visited:
                    area = dfs(r,c)
                    max_area = max(max_area,area)
        return max_area
                    
